# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SalonBook client environment variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file contains NAMES ONLY. Every value is intentionally empty.
#
# How to use it locally:
#   1. Copy this file:  cp .env.example .env.local
#   2. Fill .env.local with your local values.
#   3. Never commit .env.local, .env, or any other real env file.
#
# Why the values are empty here:
#   GitHub, hosting logs, and browser bundles are not safe places for secrets.
#   The .gitignore already ignores .env*, so a real env file cannot be committed
#   by mistake. This tracked example is only a checklist for developers.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public origin of the Express REST API.
# Use ONLY the origin here (scheme + host + optional port), for example a local
# server origin or a deployed server origin. Do NOT append "/api" here.
#
# The client code appends its own paths such as /api/services, and the Better
# Auth client appends /api/auth. Keeping this as an origin only prevents double
# "/api/api" paths.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means Next.js inlines this value into the browser JavaScript
# bundle. That is required for browser-side fetch(), but it also means this
# variable must never contain a password, secret key, or token.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# Public URL of the Better Auth server.
# The server uses this to build OAuth callbacks and trusted URLs. The browser
# cannot read a non-NEXT_PUBLIC variable, so this client does NOT consume it
# directly; it is listed because deployment and the assignment require the name.
# Keep it here as documentation, and set the real value in the hosting settings.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=

# Optional public Google OAuth client ID.
# Better Auth performs the Google redirect on the Express server, so the client
# normally does not need this value. It is included because the brief asks for
# the name of any public Google client ID the auth client needs.
#
# NEVER put GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET here. A client secret must stay on the server.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
